ratpoints_gpu
=============

Copyright (C) 2026 Samuel J. Li

ratpoints_gpu is an independent CUDA implementation for bounded rational-point
searches on hyperelliptic curves. No source code from ratpoints was copied,
adapted, or referenced in its development.

The algorithmic approach and command-line conventions were informed by:

  Michael Stoll, "Documentation for the ratpoints program,"
  arXiv:0803.3165.

ratpoints, developed by Michael Stoll, is a separate project:
  https://github.com/MichaelStollBayreuth/ratpoints

ratpoints_gpu is not affiliated with or endorsed by Michael Stoll or the
ratpoints project.

